              <FunctionalConsequenceComment>Modifies an exonic cryptic donor site at NC_000022.10:g.30823197 from -1.79 to 1.80 bits. Significant p-values: junction spanning - intron inclusion (27 reads, p=0.0134), read abundance - intron inclusion (1898 reads, p=0.0387). Computations were originally performed using genomic coordinates. This variant was mapped to an appropriate current MANE database designation or, if not present in this source, to the longest relevant transcript in the Biocommons Universal Transcript Archive using the hgvs Python package. The original genomic coordinate was based on GRCh37 and was submitted as an "Alternate designation". Modifications of Figure 2 of PMID:31275557 for ClinVar: a) "strongly corroborating Veridical p-value" refers to "junction-spanning" evidence types; b) add the text "and natural site &lt; 300 nucleotides away?" to "Ri,final &gt; nearest natural site Ri"; c) "Aberrant" and "Likely aberrant" classifications are now both defined as "Functionally abnormal" (analogous to ACMG/AMP reporting); d) "Allele-specific alternative splicing" classification now defined as "Function uncertain" (based on results for similar variants in PMID: 32211018); e) average heterozygosity based-criteria no longer contribute to classification.</FunctionalConsequenceComment>
              <Result>junction spanning - intron inclusion (p=0.0134),read abundance - intron inclusion (p=0.0387)</Result>
